Modifications: every one of the file's 283,688 records is kept (none is
marked invisible, none lacks a position or a temperature). Of each, only
the herd's identifier (the collar's), the time, the collar's temperature
(whole degrees Celsius, as recorded) and the position (rounded to five
decimal places, about a metre) are kept. The time is moved from UTC to
South African Standard Time, two hours ahead, so the map reads local
time. The map's SQL joins each herd's fixes into stretches of one
temperature band and measures each stretch's straight-line distance,
duration and speed.


